Overview
APT35 is an Iranian state-aligned threat group focused on espionage through phishing and credential theft.

Primary Objectives
- Intelligence collection
- Long-term email account access
- Targeted phishing campaigns

Target Sectors
- Government
- Academia
- Defense contractors
- Journalists
- Human rights organizations

Key Characteristics
- Heavy reliance on phishing emails
- Fake login pages (credential harvesting)
- MFA fatigue / token abuse attempts
- Cloud-first intrusion strategy

APT35 Behavior Model

1. Phishing Entry Point
- Credential harvesting via fake login portals
- Email spoofing and impersonation campaigns

2. Credential Replay
- Reuse of stolen passwords
- Password spraying against cloud services

3. Cloud Account Abuse
- Gmail / O365 mailbox access
- Forwarding rules creation
- OAuth token abuse

4. Identity Anomalies
- Impossible travel logins
- New device login patterns
- MFA bypass attempts

Detection Principle

"If the identity is compromised, endpoint telemetry may remain clean."
